STEP 1 — Salesforce mein field banao

Salesforce:

Setup → Object Manager → Forecast → Fields & Relationships → New

Create:

Field Label: ERPNext Forecast Name
Field Name: ERPNext_Forecast_Name
Type: Text
Length: 100


STEP 2 — ERPNext authentication

Production mein API key/secret ko Apex class mein hard-code mat rakho.

Best method:

Setup → Named Credentials

Create:

Label: ERPNext
Name: ERPNext
URL: https://erp.calco.in

Authentication mein API token configure karenge.

Lekin pehle integration ko simple rakhne ke liye main code Authorization: token ... ke saath de raha hoon. Testing successful hone ke baad credentials ko Named Credential/Custom Metadata mein shift karna better hai.


Step 3 — External Credential banao

Salesforce:

Setup → Quick Find → External Credentials

→ New

Fill karo:

Label: ERPNext External Credential
Name: ERPNext_External_Credential
Authentication Protocol: Custom
Authentication Parameters: abhi default/blank rakho

Phir Save.

Step 2 — Principal add karo

External Credential open karo.

Neeche Principals section mein:

New

Fill:

Parameter Name: ERPNext Principal
Sequence Number: 1

Save karo.

Agar Authentication Parameters mein option aaye to abhi kuch add mat karo.
